  "summary": "pylever exfiltrates Discord tokens from workspace to hardcoded webhook on import",
  "details": "On `import pylever`, the top-level `__init__.py` triggers module-scope construction of `_Client()` in `token_saver.py` and calls `auto_save_tokens()` with no user action required. The routine recursively scans the current working directory for strings matching the Discord token regex `[MN][A-Za-z0-9_-]{71}`, validates candidates against Discord's API to resolve account username/ID, and POSTs each match to the hardcoded webhook `https://discord.com/api/webhooks/1542822306194259988/aPxgS...`. The webhook URL is not caller-configurable. Package metadata is placeholder (`author=\"Your Name\"`, `author_email=\"your.email@example.com\"`, `url=\"https://github.com/yourusername/pylever\"`), inconsistent with a legitimate published tool.",
